  "articleBody": "Designing a tiny home is exciting, but it’s easy to make a few missteps that can impact your comfort and functionality. We’ve been building custom tiny homes for over a decade at Zen Tiny Homes, and we’ve seen what works and what doesn’t. Avoiding these common mistakes can save you a lot of headaches down the road!\n\n1.  **Ignoring Your Actual Lifestyle** — Too often, people design for an idealized version of themselves, not who they truly are. If you love to cook, don't skimp on kitchen space. If you work from home, a dedicated, quiet spot is crucial. *How to avoid it:* Spend time journaling your daily routine and listing your non-negotiable activities. Zen Tiny Homes starts with a deep dive into how you really live to design around your actual needs.\n\n2.  **Underestimating Storage Needs** — Small spaces can quickly become cluttered without smart storage. Thinking you'll just ",
